{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Many.</b> Rabbi Moses said: one who does not set his heart to keep His ways — perhaps his steps slipped, and on this account he is called wicked. It is also possible that it refers to one burdened with transgression." "And the meaning of <b>but one who trusts in HaShem</b> — that he not rely on physicians like Asa. And know that Scripture permitted healing only from the wound of a person, for HaShem alone is the healer of Israel, and His healing is to strengthen a person's soul and to increase his fear [of Heaven]."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:29:14.392020950Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}